==English==
{{wp|Management}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|managah|managuh||eye dialect}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:af|manage|-er<id:agent noun>|tree=1|text=+}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmæn.ɪ.dʒə/|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-manager.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmæn.ə.dʒəɹ/|[ˈmeə̯n.ə.d͡ʒɚ]|a=GA}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-manager.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|a=North India|/mæːˈneː.dʒə(r)/|/ˈmæː.nə.dʒə(r)/}}
* {{IPA|en|a=South India|/ˈmæː.ne(ː).dʒə(r)/}}
* {{hyph|en|man|a|ger}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|management}} A person whose job is to [[manage]] something, such as a business, a restaurant, or a sports team.
#: {{syn|en|administrator|boss|chief|controller|comptroller|foreman|head|head man|overseer|organizer|superintendent|supervisor}}
#: {{ux|en|the position of marketing '''manager'''}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2013-09-01|author=w:Phil McNulty|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/23830980|work=w:BBC Sport|text=And it was a fitting victory for Liverpool as {{w|Anfield}} celebrated the 100th anniversary of the birth of their legendary Scottish '''manager''' {{w|Bill Shankly}}.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20150325063804/http://www.bbc.co.uk:80/sport/0/football/23830980|archivedate=25 March 2015}}
# {{lb|en|baseball|association football}} The [[head coach]].
# {{lb|en|music}} An [[administrator]], for a singer or group. {{rfex|en}} <!--why not same as sense 1?-->
# {{lb|en|software}} A [[window]] or [[application]] whose purpose is to give the user the control over some aspect of the system.
#: {{ux|en|a [[file manager|file '''manager''']]; a [[task manager|task '''manager''']]; {{w|Program Manager|Program '''Manager'''}}}}

